5	 * contained in the owner's {@code customerCode}.
6	 *
7	 * <p>Non-digit characters (the separators in {@code '<CITY3>-<LAST3>-<NNNN>'}) are ignored. The
8	 * digits are processed right-to-left, doubling every second digit starting with the rightmost;
9	 * a doubled value above nine has nine subtracted. The check digit is the amount that brings the
10	 * running sum up to the next multiple of ten.
11	 */
12	public final class CheckDigit {
13	
